{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>And you shall destroy all their molten images.</b> It is found in Midrash: the verse says מלפנו etc. — מלפנו, from the beasts of the earth. The Holy One, blessed be He, teaches us from the mule of Elijah etc. Immediately Elijah built an altar, and it is written: ויעש תעלה כבית סאתים. I heard: like the courtyard of the Mishkan, and this is what they said: in every place, se'atayim is like the courtyard of the Mishkan. And it is written: מלאו ארבעה כדים מים — and they repeated and tripled, and the trench was full of water. And how was it filled with these jugs? Rather, Elisha his disciple came and poured water upon the hand of Elijah, and his two hands became like two springs, and from them the trench was filled. And this is what the verse says: הנה פה אלישע בן שפט אשר יצק מים על ידי אליהו. ומעוף השמים תחכמנו — from the ravens that sustained Elijah, bringing him bread and meat in the morning and bread and meat in the evening; and they would bring to him from the house of Jehoshaphat, and they did not want to enter the house of Ahab to bring from there, because of the idolatry that was in his house. And it appears to me that this is not as the version in the Talmud in פרק ראשון דחולין, which concludes: והעורבים מביאים לו etc., and Rabbi Yehuda said in the name of Rav: from the slaughterhouse of Ahab."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The opening phrase מלפנו וכו' likely alludes to a verse (possibly Job 18:21 or similar) whose citation is abbreviated; rendered as it stands. The chain of midrashic anecdotes linking Elijah's miracles to phrases in this verse is translated hyper-literally without reconstructing missing context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:33.074149801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}